    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483-a1">

                <pb facs="0608" n="506" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg506"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador O’Brien to the Minister for Foreign
                        Affairs.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-05-02"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">May 2, 1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 105.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Monsieur le Ministre</hi>: I am this moment in
                    receipt of a cablegram from the Secretary of State asking me to convey the
                    sympathy of the President and Government of the United States with the Japanese
                    Government in the terrible disaster resulting from the explosion on the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Matsushima</hi>. In performing this office, I desire to
                    give expression to my own sincere regret for the sad occurrence and my genuine
                    sympathy with those to whom it has brought loss and sorrow.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. J. O’Brien.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
